MID_EV30_000_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_000_m01_036: 
MID_EV30_000_m01_037: 
MID_EV30_000_m01_001: With that done, this seems a fine place for me\nto rest.
MID_EV30_000_m01_002: I ought to save my strength for the work to come.
MID_EV30_000_m01_003: You'll have to shoulder the lion's share of the fights,\nin other words.
MID_EV30_000_m01_004: <NCA>"Got it."
MID_EV30_000_m01_005: <NCB>"But I was counting on you..."
MID_EV30_000_m01_006: <ACA>Hmhm. I like that you require so little convincing.
MID_EV30_000_m01_007: <ACB>Why would one with such a strapping body require\naid from a meager bird?
MID_EV30_000_m01_008: This shoulder of yours is quite comfortable. I could\nperch here all day. Hmhmhm!
MID_EV30_000_m01_009: But worry not. When the time comes, you shall see\nmy power on full display.
MID_EV30_000_m01_010: I'd heard some news of what to expect, but it didn't\nprepare me for the state of things here.
MID_EV30_000_m01_011: There are no signs of life anywhere. The underworld\nhas swallowed the city whole.
MID_EV30_000_m01_012: *wince*
MID_EV30_000_m01_013: The vast majority of the people who lived here were\nfed to Dagda's cauldron.
MID_EV30_000_m01_014: That's what led to the underworld gate opening. It's\nnot just the city at risk—it's the whole continent.
MID_EV30_000_m01_015: The risen dead streaming from these gates have\nreached every corner of the land by now.
MID_EV30_000_m01_016: Every day, there are fewer survivors and more souls\nsent to the underworld to join their forces.
MID_EV30_000_m01_017: Will dwelling on past mistakes rectify the problem?\nI think not.
MID_EV30_000_m01_018: Our most pressing task is to approach the gate to\nthe underworld and destroy it.
MID_EV30_000_m01_019: You recall its location, yes?
MID_EV30_000_m01_020: <NCA>"I remember."
MID_EV30_000_m01_021: <NCB>"Remind me."
MID_EV30_000_m01_022: <ACA>Indeed, 'tis directly below Dagda's cauldron.
MID_EV30_000_m01_023: <ACB>Have you forgotten? Come now. 'Tis in the hollow\ndirectly beneath Dagda's cauldron.
MID_EV30_000_m01_024: We should be on our way. Although...
MID_EV30_000_m01_025: Hrm...
MID_EV30_000_m01_026: What's wrong? You seem less sure of yourself\nthan usual.
MID_EV30_000_m01_027: Our forces are a bit thin for an assault on the gate\nto the underworld.
MID_EV30_000_m01_028: Ah well. Wishing otherwise won't make it so.
MID_EV30_000_m01_029: I had thought we wouldn't do this alone.
MID_EV30_000_m01_030: Were we supposed to be joined by those "powerful\nwarriors" you mentioned?
MID_EV30_000_m01_031: We were. But whatever the outcome of that gambit,\nwe must play out our hand.
MID_EV30_000_m01_032: By dint of the causality you have rewritten, they\nought to have survived to this day.
MID_EV30_000_m01_033: I feel sure they will fly to our side once they learn\nthat the Dagsion gate is no more.
MID_EV30_000_m01_034: Would that we could wait, but time runs short.\nLet us seize the initiative.
MID_EV30_000_m01_035: No more dallying! Onward to Dagda's cauldron!
MID_EV30_039_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_039_m01_001: Wait!
MID_EV30_039_m01_002: I know it's time we began pushing back against the\narmies of the underworld.
MID_EV30_039_m01_003: But I have a question for you first.
MID_EV30_039_m01_004: Fortuna told me you are partially responsible for\nthis catastrophe.
MID_EV30_039_m01_005: I have to know. Is that true?
MID_EV30_039_m01_006: <NCA>"What if it is?"
MID_EV30_039_m01_007: <NCB>"I don't know."
MID_EV30_039_m01_008: *wince*
MID_EV30_039_m01_009: Hong Hua? Why bring this up now?
MID_EV30_039_m01_010: I'm not asking so I can pin the blame on you. For I...\nplayed my own part in this.
MID_EV30_039_m01_011: Long ago, during the Battle of Fezzan, I was gravely\nwounded. They killed my husband and took my child.
MID_EV30_039_m01_012: The boy was barely five years old when they brought\nhim to Dagsion as a prisoner.
MID_EV30_039_m01_013: <NCA>"What happened to him?"
MID_EV30_039_m01_014: <NCB>"What did you do then?"
MID_EV30_039_m01_015: <ACA>I never learned that, though I searched for him\ndesperately.
MID_EV30_039_m01_016: <ACA>To this day I don't know if he died in Dagda's\ncauldron or if he found refuge in Damascar.
MID_EV30_039_m01_017: <ACB>I lived a life fueled by anger and hatred.
MID_EV30_039_m01_018: <ACB>But I never stopped praying that my son found his\nway to Damascar.
MID_EV30_039_m01_019: My loathing of the Divine Emperor never faded.\nBut my son's face is gone from my memory.
MID_EV30_039_m01_020: Heh. Sad, isn't it, that my hatred was so much\nstronger than my love.
MID_EV30_039_m01_021: I'm only alive today because my husband's Heart\nCore was transplanted to me after his death.
MID_EV30_039_m01_022: Once I recovered, I infiltrated Dagsion to get my\nrevenge on Dagda the Great.
MID_EV30_039_m01_023: And I failed at that too. I narrowly escaped with my\nlife from the botched assassination.
MID_EV30_039_m01_024: It was Magistra Raksha who saved me. She said our\ngoals aligned, and I worked with her for a long time.
MID_EV30_039_m01_025: Those pretty words had me dancing on her strings,\nbut they were all a lie.
MID_EV30_039_m01_026: Her schemes have resulted in the deaths of a million\ninnocent citizens of Dagsion.
MID_EV30_039_m01_027: Men and women, old and young...many children who\nwould have been my son's age.
MID_EV30_039_m01_028: I didn't want any of that...but I'm still complicit.
MID_EV30_039_m01_029: I know that the dead will never forgive me.
MID_EV30_039_m01_030: Just as I could never forgive the Divine Emperor.
MID_EV30_039_m01_031: I know that those who have been lost can never\nreturn to us.
MID_EV30_039_m01_032: But Master Zenon told me to save as many of the\nliving as I can anyway. So I hold tight to that idea.
MID_EV30_039_m01_033: I hope...I hope that can be my atonement. My sins\nwill follow me forever. But maybe...maybe...
MID_EV30_039_m01_034: <NCA>"I know how you feel."
MID_EV30_039_m01_035: *sniffle* Thank you. I needed you to know.
MID_EV30_039_m01_036: I'm ready to go now. Let's get started saving\nthe world.
MID_EV30_001_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_001_m01_001: *yawn* What now? Mm. This is all so tiresome...
MID_EV30_001_m01_002: Ugh. Not what I expected from the guardian\nof the gate.
MID_EV30_001_m01_003: Hm? How low he's fallen.
MID_EV30_001_m01_004: I don't recall inviting visitors. I expect you're here\nfor the gate.
MID_EV30_001_m01_005: That's right. I don't know who you are, but we've\ncome to clean up this mess.
MID_EV30_001_m01_006: A crew of lowly humans, come to destroy the gate\nBalor told me to guard.
MID_EV30_001_m01_007: I don't think you've thought this through. Doesn't the\nidea strike you as arrogant?
MID_EV30_001_m01_008: Of all possible gates to approach, you choose mine.\nYou must be out of your minds.
MID_EV30_001_m01_009: And only three against me? I believe you are\noutnumbered.
MID_EV30_001_m01_010: <NCA>"We're enough to deal with you."
MID_EV30_001_m01_011: <NCB>"You might be right."
MID_EV30_001_m01_012: <ACA>You should know better than to spout\nempty platitudes.
MID_EV30_001_m01_013: <ACB>Hm. At least one of you can see what you're\nup against.
MID_EV30_001_m01_014: Fine. If it will shut your impudent mouths, I'll give\nyou the battle you seek.
MID_EV30_001_m01_015: Unbelievable that I'm expected to deal with such\nfools personally...
MID_EV30_001_m01_016: Aaagh. It's all so tiresome I could die.
MID_EV30_001_m01_017: Rrraaah!
MID_EV30_001_m01_018: Aah! Ngh... The pressure coming from him\nis unreal...
MID_EV30_001_m01_019: Be careful, Promised One! Whoever this is, he's\nstronger than he looks.
MID_EV30_001_m01_020: The finest women and choicest meats—all tiresome.\nPleasure holds no meaning for me anymore.
MID_EV30_001_m01_021: Everything I desired in life...all that once drove me...\nIt's all such a bore!
MID_EV30_001_m01_022: Hyah!
MID_EV30_002_m01_001: That was a swift strike. You have more nerve than\nI gave you credit for.
MID_EV30_002_m01_002: Impossible. You're the Divine Emperor?!
MID_EV30_002_m01_003: Heh. Even stooping to pick up my helmet is too\nmuch effort.
MID_EV30_002_m01_004: Poor thing. For all his many flaws, he was once\na Founder.
MID_EV30_002_m01_005: 'Tis a pity he has bent the knee to that\ndamned Balor.
MID_EV30_002_m01_006: You... I can tell you're no mere bird. Something is\noff about you...
MID_EV30_002_m01_007: I can't put my finger on it...but it's not worth thinking\nabout anyway.
MID_EV30_002_m01_008: I didn't suspect the Brimstone Lord under that armor\nwas you. But it works out well for me.
MID_EV30_002_m01_009: You may be dead, but I won't pass up the chance to\navenge what you did to my kin.
MID_EV30_002_m01_010: Oh? You think you have a chance? Hmhm. We'll see.
MID_EV30_002_m01_011: No more games. It's time I took this seriously. In the\nend, it doesn't matter who you are.
MID_EV30_002_m01_012: For no one can stand against me with the power of\nthe underworld on my side. Least of all you!
MID_EV30_002_m01_013: RRRAAAGH!
MID_EV30_002_m01_014: Harnessing the power of the underworld to fuel his\ntransformation? What a cheat.
MID_EV30_002_m01_015: You'll regret making me put in this effort. Before I'm\nthrough, you'll long for death!
MID_EV30_040_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_040_m01_035: 
MID_EV30_040_m01_036: 
MID_EV30_040_m01_001: Rrgh. This insolence...will not stand.
MID_EV30_040_m01_002: I've never even seen you before. I demand to know\nwho you are.
MID_EV30_040_m01_003: <NCA>Say nothing.
MID_EV30_040_m01_004: Ah! W-wait...no. You can't be...
MID_EV30_040_m01_005: No... Nothing else makes sense. But this doesn't\nmake sense either!
MID_EV30_040_m01_006: Heh heh heh... Well, enjoy your victory for now.
MID_EV30_040_m01_007: All this means for me is a short stay in the\nunderworld.
MID_EV30_040_m01_008: Soon I'll grow as strong as I ever was—no, stronger!\nAnd then I'll be right back here.
MID_EV30_040_m01_009: So savor this moment while you still can.
MID_EV30_040_m01_010: Ah! Is this true?
MID_EV30_040_m01_032: <NCA>"Is he right?"
MID_EV30_040_m01_037: 
MID_EV30_040_m01_011: I'm afraid so. From here, he'll slink away into the\ndepths of the underworld for Balor to renew him.
MID_EV30_040_m01_012: All the risen dead of the underworld—including this\nwastrel—are Balor's loyal hounds.
MID_EV30_040_m01_013: Until we defeat Balor, who reigns above them all,\nand fully eradicate the underworld...
MID_EV30_040_m01_014: he will come into his power again and return to\nplague our world.
MID_EV30_040_m01_015: But...if that's true, then no matter how many times\nwe win, he can never truly be defeated.
MID_EV30_040_m01_038: 
MID_EV30_040_m01_033: <NCA>"Is there nothing we can do?"
MID_EV30_040_m01_039: 
MID_EV30_040_m01_016: Under normal circumstances, yes. But this time\nshall be an exception.
MID_EV30_040_m01_017: I have instructions from her to ensure that he in\nparticular does not escape.
MID_EV30_040_m01_018: You're...Fortuna? Damn you. You're nothing but a\npale copy of the progenitor god.
MID_EV30_040_m01_019: I forbid you to find sanctuary in the underworld.\nThrough me, you shall be delivered to her.
MID_EV30_040_m01_020: No...no! I don't want to go back to the progenitor\ngod. Don't send me back to Mother!
MID_EV30_040_m01_021: Mother will be furious when she learns of the\nstate of the land of Dagda...
MID_EV30_040_m01_022: Indeed she will! Perhaps you should have thought of\nthat before you ran roughshod over it.
MID_EV30_040_m01_023: Please don't do this... I'm begging you to look the\nother way for me!
MID_EV30_040_m01_024: Fool! Do you still not grasp what your undue fear of\nher has wrought?
MID_EV30_040_m01_025: All would be well, had you not allowed Balor's\ndaughters to prey on that terror!
MID_EV30_040_m01_026: Go and grovel for mercy at her feet.
MID_EV30_040_m01_027: No... No, no, no... I don't want to! I won't!
MID_EV30_040_m01_028: NOOOOOOOOO!
MID_EV30_040_m01_029: He's...gone. Does this mean he won't be back?
MID_EV30_040_m01_034: <NCA>"Is it over, then?"
MID_EV30_040_m01_030: *sigh* 'Tis precisely what it means.
MID_EV30_040_m01_031: Never shall that boor stain this world with his\npresence again.
MID_EV30_003_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_003_m01_001: Well! 'Tis a promising start.
MID_EV30_003_m01_002: Look. The clouds over Dagsion have cleared, letting\nthe sun's light through.
MID_EV30_003_m01_003: I can't remember the last time I saw such a clear sky.\nIt's almost too bright.
MID_EV30_003_m01_042: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_004: <NCA>"It's beautiful."
MID_EV30_003_m01_005: <NCB>"This is only the beginning."
MID_EV30_003_m01_006: <ACA>You're right. I'd almost forgotten how lovely it\ncould be.
MID_EV30_003_m01_007: <ACA>Strange to feel so grateful for what I once took\nfor granted.
MID_EV30_003_m01_008: <ACB>Right you are. This is bigger than just Dagsion.
MID_EV30_003_m01_009: <ACB>We can't rest until the skies over all of Dagda\nare clear again.
MID_EV30_003_m01_010: How astonishing that we overcame that monster\nwith our meager forces.
MID_EV30_003_m01_011: You are redoubtable warriors indeed, but I wonder\nif we few can finish the work.
MID_EV30_003_m01_012: 'Tis well enough. Should we need reinforcements,\nwe can always revisit the Obelisk Chamber.
MID_EV30_003_m01_013: There we will find new avenues to explore, should\nwe require them.
MID_EV30_003_m01_052: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_044: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_045: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_046: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_047: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_048: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_049: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_050: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_051: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_014: Before we set off, I ought to convey my thanks to\nyou for hastening to our side.
MID_EV30_003_m01_015: I am called Fortuna, though my true name is the\nVoice upon the Peak.
MID_EV30_003_m01_016: I am among the children of the progenitor god Sothis,\nwho is The Beginning.
MID_EV30_003_m01_017: 'Twas she who sent me to this land.
MID_EV30_003_m01_018: It is good that you have bested the adversities of\ncausality to be here today.
MID_EV30_003_m01_019: You doubtless have many questions for me and my\nassociate here.
MID_EV30_003_m01_020: But there will be idle moments later for you to ask\nthem. For now, we must act.
MID_EV30_003_m01_021: <NCA>"It's good to see you again."
MID_EV30_003_m01_043: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_022: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_023: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_024: I came here as quickly as I could—not quickly\nenough, it seems.
MID_EV30_003_m01_025: But I did tell you I'd repay you, and now I can\ndo just that.
MID_EV30_003_m01_026: It's been a while, white bird. From now on, I'll fight\nby your side.
MID_EV30_003_m01_027: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_028: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_029: A queen of Saramis never forgets a debt incurred.\nAs repayment, my arm is yours to command.
MID_EV30_003_m01_030: I have long waited for this. I am glad we meet again.
MID_EV30_003_m01_031: As I said I would, I will again lend my blade to\nyour fight.
MID_EV30_003_m01_032: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_033: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_034: 
MID_EV30_003_m01_035: I know there is much to catch up on, but come.\nOur work is urgent.
MID_EV30_003_m01_036: <NCA>"What's our first move?"
MID_EV30_003_m01_037: Hmhmhm. I should have thought that was obvious.
MID_EV30_003_m01_038: We must spread the joyous news that salvation is at\nhand to every corner of Dagda!
MID_EV30_003_m01_039: 'Twill lift their spirits to know that the one promised\nto them has arrived.
MID_EV30_003_m01_040: And not only arrived, but already liberated Dagsion\nfrom the forces of the underworld.
MID_EV30_003_m01_041: A new flame of hope for Dagda has been lit this day.
MID_NR30_00_m01: <SH>
MID_NR30_00_m01_001: Dagdan Imperial Calendar, year 1454.
MID_NR30_00_m01_002: At the start of a new year, the Promised One arrived\nin Dagsion and destroyed its underworld gate.
MID_NR30_00_m01_003: It was the first bright ray in a land that had been\ndarkened by despair.
MID_NR30_00_m01_004: The good news spread throughout all of Dagda,\nfrom survivor to survivor, stoking a small flame\nof hope in each person's heart.
MID_NR30_00_m01_005: People had clung to life desperately. They'd lived in\nconstant fear of death on their doorstep. The news\nseemed too good to be true, but still, it brought\na sense of great relief, even joy.
MID_NR30_00_m01_006: One by one, they began to move, despite the danger.
MID_NR30_00_m01_007: They made their way to the imperial capital of\nDagsion, now a sanctuary for the living.
MID_NR30_00_m01_008: And they brought their hope with them—flame after\ntiny flame—which gathered into a bright bonfire.\nThe people felt the spirit of resistance once more.
MID_NR30_00_m01_009: —Saint Cichol, "The Underworld War,"\nPart 1, Chapter 4
MID_EV30_100_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_100_m01_047: 
MID_EV30_100_m01_001: GYAAGH!
MID_EV30_100_m01_002: Whew... Was that the last of them? I have to make\nsure that not one of them escapes.
MID_EV30_100_m01_003: Well done, Aurora. It seems we defeated all of them\nthis time.
MID_EV30_100_m01_004: Please, Centurio. I'm no longer one of the divines.\nYou shouldn't use that name.
MID_EV30_100_m01_005: Perhaps. But old habits are hard to break.
MID_EV30_100_m01_006: Especially for a man my age—a stubborn man\nat that.
MID_EV30_100_m01_007: But if you refer to me as a goddess in front of others,\nit'll make them nervous around me.
MID_EV30_100_m01_008: And that would be a shame since I finally got them\nto accept me.
MID_EV30_100_m01_009: You are correct. I will act with prudence.
MID_EV30_100_m01_010: By the way, I do not see Cai today. Where is he?
MID_EV30_100_m01_011: He... It seems he had to go somewhere a little\nwhile back.
MID_EV30_100_m01_012: Well, knowing him, even if he runs into trouble, he'll\nhandle it just fine.
MID_EV30_100_m01_013: How much longer will this trouble go on? It's been\nfour years since the underworld gates appeared.
MID_EV30_100_m01_014: My power is barely enough to protect Ribeira from\nthe risen dead.
MID_EV30_100_m01_015: Even so, our crops don't grow well under this sky.\nHow long can we hold out?
MID_EV30_100_m01_016: Are we just waiting until everyone's strength fails?
MID_EV30_100_m01_017: It seems that the surviving divines are each opposing\nthe underworld's armies at their individual temples.
MID_EV30_100_m01_018: I hear that this has been the greatest solace for those\nliving in the surrounding areas.
MID_EV30_100_m01_019: But the temples are so far apart. It's hard for them to\ncoordinate with any real effect.
MID_EV30_100_m01_020: If only we could take back Dagsion, we might be able\nto mount a resistance.
MID_EV30_100_m01_021: Is it even possible for human hands to destroy an\nunderworld gate?
MID_EV30_100_m01_022: I have heard that people rallied to attempt it several\ntimes, and each time they failed.
MID_EV30_100_m01_023: But unless someone succeeds, we're all just waiting\nfor our destruction.
MID_EV30_100_m01_024: If that's the case, I ought to...
MID_EV30_100_m01_025: Father. Mother. Please, grant me courage.
MID_EV30_100_m01_026: Aurora! Something has happened.
MID_EV30_100_m01_027: "Aurora"? You too, chief? As I've told you before,\nI am no longer in the position of a goddess.
MID_EV30_100_m01_028: Just Laura will suffice. Now, what has happened?
MID_EV30_100_m01_029: Something unbelievable.
MID_EV30_100_m01_030: A savior appeared in Dagsion and destroyed the gate\nof the underworld!
MID_EV30_100_m01_031: Who would be capable of such a feat? Tell me, who\nis this savior?
MID_EV30_100_m01_032: All I know is that they were clad in pure white and\naccompanied by a bird.
MID_EV30_100_m01_033: But the rumors are spreading now, invigorating\nthe survivors across Dagda.
MID_EV30_100_m01_034: People are flocking to Dagsion from all over to join\nthe savior.
MID_EV30_100_m01_035: Could Cai have left to join this person?
MID_EV30_100_m01_036: Ah...
MID_EV30_100_m01_037: Centurio, all this time I've been thinking about\nwhether there is anything I can do to help.
MID_EV30_100_m01_038: I have wondered whether, as a god, I ought to\nreturn to my temple.
MID_EV30_100_m01_039: Perhaps by doing so I could help everyone.
MID_EV30_100_m01_040: I have been waiting to hear those words from your\nlips, Aurora.
MID_EV30_100_m01_041: People need hope. It is precisely in times such as\nthese that faith holds power.
MID_EV30_100_m01_042: If you return to your temple, you would become\na light and an encouragement to many.
MID_EV30_100_m01_043: But what about this village?
MID_EV30_100_m01_044: Fortunately, the former vulkan Nightblossom Estie\nalso lives here.
MID_EV30_100_m01_045: She may have retired from active duty, but her skills\nare sharp. We can trust her.
MID_EV30_100_m01_046: I will prepare for our immediate departure\nto Dagsion.